{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Adopt existing Spring Framework patterns: dependency injection, auto-configuration, and the binder abstraction already used in Spring Cloud Stream.",
    "Implement U1 (Azure Event Hubs) as a new Spring Cloud Stream binder on top of the official Azure SDK for Java (com.microsoft.azure:azure-eventhubs), reusing the Kafka binder structure as a template.",
    "Implement U2 (IPython Notebook) via the Jupyter kernel gateway protocol over WebSockets, exposing Spring XD shell commands as a kernel so notebooks can drive the same DSL.",
    "Implement U4 (direct binding) as an in-JVM binder profile that wires producer/consumer modules directly via functional beans, without an external broker.",
    "Implement U5 (REST APIs for xd-admin) using Spring MVC on top of the existing xd-admin server, exposing CRUD endpoints backed by the ModuleRegistry (U6).",
    "Implement U6 (ModuleRegistry stubs) as an in-memory, interface-driven mock that conforms to the existing ModuleRegistry contract, enabling isolated testing of REST endpoints.",
    "Implement U7 (repository migration) as a Git history-preserving move of the spring-cloud-stream-modules project into the spring-cloud-dataflow organization, updating parent POMs, CI configs, and issue links.",
    "Implement U8 (in-memory stream definition repository) as a ConcurrentHashMap-backed implementation of the StreamDefinitionRepository interface, selected via a deployment property to avoid persisting state.",
    "Implement U3 (upgrade preservation) as a migration step in the admin server bootstrap that copies legacy servers.yml and module directories into a versioned backup location before applying the new layout."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single experienced Java/Spring developer will implement all activities (no team parallelism).",
    "The Spring XD and Spring Cloud DataFlow codebases are already available locally and the build infrastructure (Maven/Gradle, CI) is already configured.",
    "Azure Event Hubs credentials and a test namespace are available for development and integration testing.",
    "IPython/Jupyter integration is limited to read/write of the existing Spring XD shell commands; a full notebook UI is out of scope.",
    "The REST API surface for U5 follows the endpoints already informally documented in Spring XD (streams, jobs, modules) and does not introduce a new API contract.",
    "Module migration in U7 keeps Git history using git filter-branch or a similar tool and does not require new module functionality beyond relocation.",
    "One workday equals 8 productive hours; no calendar time, meetings, or onboarding overhead is included.",
    "No major refactor of existing Spring XD core is required; changes are additive or interface-based."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and design",
      "activity_description": "Review the eight user stories, identify cross-cutting concerns (U6 feeding U5, U1 binder contract, U4 bypass architecture), produce a short design note covering module/package layout, interface changes, and sequencing of the remaining activities."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Azure Event Hubs binder implementation",
      "activity_description": "Create a new spring-cloud-stream-binder-azure-eventhubs module: EventHubsBinderConfiguration, EventHubsMessageChannelBinder, EventHubsProducer, and EventHubsConsumer using the Azure Event Hubs Java SDK, including partition handling, checkpointing, and connection settings."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2 - IPython Notebook integration",
      "activity_description": "Add an IPython/Jupyter kernel implementation for the Spring XD shell, expose it through an embedded kernel gateway endpoint, and provide a sample notebook that exercises the XD DSL commands."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Upgrade mechanism preserving legacy configuration",
      "activity_description": "Implement an admin-server bootstrap step that detects an existing installation, copies the legacy servers.yml and module directories into a timestamped backup folder, and then applies the new layout so users can manually migrate configuration."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Direct module binding (no messaging middleware)",
      "activity_description": "Introduce a 'direct' binder mode that wires producer and consumer modules in the same JVM using a direct in-memory channel, avoiding any external broker; include configuration property, factory bean, and lifecycle handling."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5 - REST APIs for xd-admin CRUD on pipelines",
      "activity_description": "Add Spring MVC controllers and DTOs for create/read/update/delete of streams, jobs, and modules, delegating persistence and module resolution to the ModuleRegistry interface (U6) and stream definition repository (U8)."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6 - ModuleRegistry stubs",
      "activity_description": "Create an in-memory ModuleRegistry implementation behind the existing ModuleRegistry interface, supporting register, lookup, and unregister of modules so REST endpoints (U5) and tests can be exercised without a real registry."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Move spring-cloud-stream-modules to s-c-d repo",
      "activity_description": "Migrate the spring-cloud-stream-modules project into the spring-cloud-dataflow organization: relocate sources while preserving history, update parent POMs, README, CI configuration, and any module coordinate references used by other components."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8 - In-memory stream definition repository",
      "activity_description": "Implement an InMemoryStreamDefinitionRepository using ConcurrentHashMap that conforms to the StreamDefinitionRepository interface, wire it as an alternative bean activated by a deployment property, and add unit tests."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Integration and end-to-end testing",
      "activity_description": "Run cross-activity integration tests: REST CRUD against the in-memory registry and repository, direct binder round-trip, Azure Event Hubs send/receive against a test namespace (if reachable), and legacy upgrade simulation. Fix any defects uncovered."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and code review polish",
      "activity_description": "Update reference docs (binder configuration for Azure, direct mode, REST endpoints, in-memory repository, upgrade procedure) and address code review comments, finalize Javadoc and changelog entries."
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 32.0
  }
}
```

